      "name": "Agelastes",
      "rank": "GENUS",
      "description": "A small genus of two guineafowl species that lack the typical spotted plumage of the family, instead having unpatterned black or grey-brown feathers. Both are forest-dwelling and more secretive than other guineafowl.",
